Slug
----

The glyph coverage in slang/text.slang (`textRootCode`,
`textSolveHoriz`, `textSolveVert`, `textCombine` and the two band loops in
`textCoverageAniso`) is a port of the Slug reference pixel shader by Eric
Lengyel, published at https://github.com/EricLengyel/Slug. The reference
shaders are offered under the MIT License (the source header states
"MIT OR Apache-2.0"), with the request that distributed use give credit:

    Slug shader code Copyright 2017 by Eric Lengyel.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0

The algorithm is described in Eric Lengyel, "GPU-Centered Font Rendering
Directly from Glyph Outlines", Journal of Computer Graphics Techniques 6(2),
2017, https://jcgt.org/published/0006/02/02/. Its patent, US 10,373,352, was
dedicated to the public domain by its author effective 17 March 2026, as
announced at https://terathon.com/blog/decade-slug.html.

The band preprocessing in text/src/bands.rs is this project's own, written
from the paper.

